{"id": "EUVD-2026-67054", "enisaUuid": "8c8ee567-cb0f-36b5-9e88-8e0c30bcbbb5", "description": "openssl_encrypt versions before 1.4.9 contain a shell injection vulnerability in the info command's reconstructed CLI block that interpolates untrusted metadata fields without quoting. Attackers can craft metadata values like pepper_name containing shell commands that execute when users copy the printed CLI block into a shell.", "datePublished": "2026-08-27T14:51:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T15:21:28", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/jahlives/openssl_encrypt/security/advisories/GHSA-gw2m-mj6q-59hc", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openssl-encrypt-before-1.4.9-shell-injection-via-info-command"], "aliases": ["PYSEC-2026-3776", "CVE-2026-81698", "GHSA-rcx3-xx7j-m3r9"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.43, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0fac7a01-9132-3c83-bc49-8934a131ac29", "product": {"name": "openssl_encrypt", "vendor": {"name": "jahlives"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.4.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "99baf09d-a82d-3e77-b2f7-04b4df303773", "vendor": {"name": "jahlives"}}], "isExploited": false}